==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.67~20 seconds<sup>20f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.67~20 seconds<sup>20f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Doge]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.67~10 seconds<sup>20f~300f</sup>.
**1 [[Hyper Mr. (Enemy)|Hyper Mr.]] spawns.
**1 [[Wall Doge]] spawns.
**1 [[Hyper Mr. (Enemy)|Hyper Mr.]] spawns.
**1 [[Wall Doge]] spawns.
**1 [[Wall Doge]] spawns.
**1 [[Hyper Mr. (Enemy)|Hyper Mr.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage is easy to beat as long as you have a long-ranged attacker and plenty of meatshields. [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], ([[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed]]) [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] can be used for long-distance striking and powerful attacks. Do not let your cats get too close to the enemy base before you have saved up enough money. Once you have a full wallet, spam everything. Make sure you always have meatshields protecting Bahamut Cat because if he dies it'll either be game over or difficult to recover.

